        "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject malformed JSON before dispatching an operation**\n\nFor the generic `operations/:operationId` endpoint, any JSON parse failure is converted to `{}` and dispatched. An authenticated caller sending truncated or otherwise malformed JSON can therefore execute operations whose schema accepts an empty object; for example, `testfn.runs.start` is a non-idempotent mutation with an empty input schema. Return `INVALID_JSON` without invoking the dispatcher, as the module-route parser already does.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
