        "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
        "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/44#discussion_r3788963506",
        "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Materialize route parameters before invoking module routes**\n\nWhen `invoke()` receives a discovered detail route such as `/resources/users/:id`, it sends the placeholder literally rather than substituting `input.id`. For GET/DELETE routes the server then extracts `:id` from the path and overwrites the real query-string ID, so the operation looks up the literal identifier `:id` and returns not found. Substitute and encode path parameters from the input before issuing the request, and apply the same behavior to `invokeRaw()`.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
      }
    },
