        "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions.next/pull/44#discussion_r3794045617",
        "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Isolate in-memory searches by tenant**\n\nWhen one `MemoryStorageAdapter` contains records for multiple `tenantId` values, this filter considers only container tags and metadata, so tenants sharing a tag—or issuing an empty-tag search—receive each other's memories. Since inserts persist `tenantId` but the search contract supplies no tenant selector, the newly functional SQLite/in-memory runtime can disclose cross-tenant content; bind the adapter per tenant or carry and enforce the tenant identity in `searchVectors`.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
